# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# This repo is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which wrote CRLF
# into the working tree while the index kept LF. Prettier defaults to
# endOfLine "lf", so every line of every CRLF file counted as a violation:
# `bun run lint` reported ~68,000 problems, of which ~67,000 were the
# carriage return alone. Real findings were unreadable underneath them.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf for these paths, so no one has to change
# their local git config for the lint script to mean something.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The sole binary asset. `text=auto` already detects it, but saying so
# explicitly means the rule above can never mangle it.
*.png binary
